								<div id="contentForThisGame_ctn">
				</div>
									<div data-panel="{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;PanelGroup&quot;}" id="aboutThisGame" class="game_page_autocollapse" style="max-height: 850px;">
						<div id="game_area_description" class="game_area_description">
							<h2>About This Game</h2>
							You expected a quiet little Halloween shop. You open the door to find its contents scattered everywhere. Time to put things right—and perhaps find out what happened.<h2 class="bb_tag" >An armful at a time</h2>Pick up scattered treasures and return them to their shelves. From curious potions and tiny familiars to pumpkins, sweets and autumn flowers, there’s a whole shop of spooky little things to sort. Enjoy the satisfaction of everything finding its place, at your own pace.<h2 class="bb_tag" >A little out of the ordinary</h2>Some things need more than tidying away. Follow strange clues, discover the shop’s secrets, and find a friend who may know something about the mess.<br><br>Settle in. There’s no timer, and you might have company.						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="game_page_autocollapse">
		<div id="game_area_content_descriptors" class="game_area_description">
			<h2>AI Generated Content Disclosure</h2>
			<p>The developers describe how their game uses AI Generated Content like this:</p>
			<p><i>
					We use generative AI across all disciplines of game development, most often with heavy amounts of human editing. That involves audio and visual art, 3D models, our logo, and localization. We use it as a productivity tool so we can achieve a higher level of quality, faster, than we would have been able to.<br />
<br />
We also have a full soundtrack of 1950's halloween pop hits that are obviously made by AI, as you can hear in the trailer. It's awesome and it'd be basically impossible otherwise. 				</i>
			</p>
					</div>
	</div>
	
				
				
